{
  "$comment": "Mow Town tuning (everything gameplay lives here, not in code). Distances in world units; the grass grid is `cell` units per cell. grass: vegetation types — resistance = cutting power needed (a tool below it chews through it slowly: chewSec[n - 1] seconds per cell when n powers short; more powers short than chewSec has entries = locked until a better mower), value = clippings per cell, height/color = uncut look, cutColor = the mowed stub. tools: the equipment path (index 0 = what the player starts with) — width = cutting width, speed = walking speed, power = cutting power, capacity = clippings the container holds, size/color = the placeholder mower (`reel`: a reel mower; otherwise a long deck on four wheels with its engine on top). upgrades: repeatable levels on top of the tool, on the shop's GEAR tab (capacity: +clippings) or BOOSTS tab (speed +share, money +share of every sale, width +units, blades +share of chewing speed on tough grass); level n costs basePrice x growth^n. boostsUnlockToolLevel: the BOOSTS tab opens with this mower. Tools with `ride` are driven: the tractor (dig's; its look, seat, exhaust and smoke: `tractor`, edited in the editor) painted by `greyscale` / `tint` (utils/Paint.ts) and scaled by `rideScale`, mounted on entering a section not restored yet. clippingPrice: money per clipping when sold. traffic: a few cars on the road tiles (right-hand lanes `lane` off the middle, `tile` grid, turning at random at junctions), stopping `gap` short of the player or the car ahead. mode: calm (just mowing) or rush (arcade layers on top: the combo), the URL's ?mode= overrides it; combo: rush's combo meter (ends `window` s after the last cut, multiplier +`step` every `stepSec` of cutting up to `max`, the extra money paid when it ends). The town's layout (sections = districts, their grass mix, bonus, stations, separators; props; pavements) is levels/town.json, edited in the editor (npm run editor).",
